@scene chapter_3b_echoing_halls

background: deep_forest.jpg
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"The road down from the Alchemist's tower narrows into a cleft in the rock, and the cleft becomes a corridor."
"Stone walls close overhead. The daylight gives up behind you."
"Ahead, the same short stretch of floor plays out again and again — footsteps that arrive without anyone walking."
"The Echoing Halls."

background: ruins.png

dialogue:
"And there he is. A man in a warden's cloak, pacing."
"Three steps forward. Three steps back. Three steps forward. His boots have worn a groove in the stone."

background: warden

npc Warden:
"Another one. Don't stand in the groove, you'll only slow me down."
"I built this corridor to guard the pass. Set myself to patrol it — forever, I thought, nobly."
"I never wrote myself a way to STOP. Now the corridor patrols ME."

npc You:
"...Can I get you out?"

npc Warden:
"Learn what I never did, traveller, and maybe. It is all here in the walls. I've had a long time to read them."

system skill_learned:
"MODULE UNLOCKED"
"THE ECHOING HALLS"
"for · range · while · accumulation · break / continue"

dialogue:
"— LESSON I — THE MARCHING STONES —"
"The Warden gestures, and a row of numbered stones lights up along the floor, one after another."

npc Warden:
"A loop is only DOING A THING, then doing it again."
"To walk a known row of stones — a fixed count — you use a FOR loop."
"And range gives you the count. But mind where range stops. It always halts one short of the number you name."

interactive: halls_march_range

npc Warden:
"You see it. range(1, 4) never sets foot on 4. The last number is a wall, not a stone."

dialogue:
"— LESSON II — THE DOOR THAT WATCHES —"
"A stone door ahead hangs half-open, trembling, as if held by a single thought."

npc Warden:
"Sometimes you do not know the count ahead of time. You only know a CONDITION."
"A WHILE loop runs and runs — but only WHILE its condition stays true."
"The moment the condition fails, the loop lets go. Watch what happens when it never can."

interactive: halls_while_countdown

npc Warden:
"That second one. No hand ever lowered the count, so the condition never turned false."
"That is my whole life, traveller, in three lines. A loop with no way to reach its end."
"So build me a better one. A loop that carries its own ending inside it."

interactive: halls_forge_exit

npc Warden:
"'while steps > 0.' When steps runs out, the loop is DONE. That is mercy, written in code."

dialogue:
"— LESSON III — THE RUNNING TOTAL —"
"As the Warden paces, a faint number hangs over his head, ticking up with every step — then resetting as he turns back."

npc Warden:
"A loop can carry something that GROWS as it goes. A count. A sum. A tally."
"Start it before the loop. Add to it each turn. When the loop ends, the total is yours."
"They call it accumulation. It is how a hundred small steps become one large answer."

interactive: halls_accumulate

dialogue:
"— LESSON IV — LEAVE, OR SKIP —"
"The Warden stops mid-stride, for the first time."

npc Warden:
"Two words can bend any loop. Learn them well; one of them is my freedom."
"BREAK leaves the loop entirely — done, out, gone."
"CONTINUE only skips the rest of this one turn, then loops on. People confuse them and pay for it."

interactive: halls_break_continue

npc Warden:
"Now forge the line I never had. The one that lets a walker LEAVE the moment he reaches the door."

interactive: halls_forge_break

npc Warden:
"'if at_door: break.' One line. One line, and I could have gone home an age ago."

dialogue:
"— LESSON V — THE CURSE ITSELF —"
"The walls around you flicker with loops — some bright and finite, some pulsing with a sick, endless light."

npc Warden:
"Here is the lesson the Blight would rather you never learned. A loop that can never end is not a loop. It is a CURSE."
"'while True' with no break. A condition nothing can turn false. Sort them, so your eye learns the difference on sight."

interactive: halls_curse_sort

npc Warden:
"Good. You can smell a trap now. That alone will save your life on the road ahead."

dialogue:
"— PROVE IT — THE CURSED DOOR —"
"The corridor rearranges into a straight run of numbered doors — first, second, third — and one of them wears a dark mark."

npc Warden:
"Walk them in order. Count them. And when you reach the marked door, do the thing I could not — STOP."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Count the doors from 1 to door_count. break the instant you reach cursed_door."

mission: halls_doors_break

background: ruins.png

dialogue:
"You open door after door, and at the marked one you simply... stop."
"The corridor exhales. It has never seen anyone stop before."

npc Warden:
"You used break, and the loop obeyed. Now. Do it for ME."

dialogue:
"— FREE THE WARDEN —"
"The Warden steps back into his worn groove, and the endless corridor stretches out ahead of him, exactly as long as it always was."

npc Warden:
"My loop runs on 'while True.' It never stops because I gave it nothing that could ever become false."
"So write me one that CAN end. Step me to the door — and let the condition run out when I arrive."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Write a while loop that steps count up to steps_to_door, then ends on its own."

mission: halls_free_warden

background: ruins.png

dialogue:
"You speak the loop."
"The Warden takes a step. Then another. Then — where always before he would have turned back — the corridor simply ENDS."
"He stands blinking at an open archway that was never there, and then always was."

background: deep_forest.jpg

npc Warden:
"...It stopped. The loop STOPPED."
"An age of pacing, and the whole of my prison was one missing condition."
"Remember that, traveller, when you meet bigger loops than me. The Blight is only this — repetition that forgot how to end."

dialogue:
"He steps through the archway into daylight, and does not pace back."
"Before he goes, he presses a worn iron whistle into your hand."

background: warden

npc Warden:
"One last thing. Prove it's yours — the whole of it — in a single breath."

interactive: halls_final_recall

npc Warden:
"While, a count that grows, and a break for the door. All of it, at once. It's yours."
"Now come and spend it. Past the archway the ground stops — the Blight ate the bridge that used to cross there."
"And a bridge is only one plank, laid again and again. You know how to say 'again' now."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Echoing Halls"
"Mastered: for · range · while · accumulation · break / continue · the infinite-loop curse"

reward:
xp: 75
gold: 40
achievement: BREAKER OF CURSES

next:
chapter_3_endless_bridge
